{
  "apiVersion": "dashboard.grafana.app/v2",
  "kind": "Dashboard",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "zarr-stats"
  },
  "spec": {
    "annotations": [
      {
        "kind": "AnnotationQuery",
        "spec": {
          "builtIn": true,
          "enable": true,
          "hide": true,
          "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
          "legacyOptions": {
            "type": "dashboard"
          },
          "name": "Annotations \u0026 Alerts",
          "query": {
            "datasource": {
              "name": "-- Grafana --"
            },
            "group": "grafana",
            "kind": "DataQuery",
            "spec": {},
            "version": "v0"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "cursorSync": "Off",
    "description": "CarbonPlan's monthly mean temperature over the Americas from a pyramided Zarr store, drawn as tiles by TiTiler; draw an area and drag the time bar to get its minimum, maximum and mean for that month.",
    "editable": true,
    "elements": {
      "panel-1": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "id": 1,
          "links": [],
          "title": "",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "# Statistics of what you draw, over a pyramided Zarr\n\nMonthly mean temperature from CarbonPlan's climate demo. **Draw** a polygon with the map's tool and **drag the time bar**: the numbers measure that area in that month.\n\nThis store is written **for maps** — a six-level pyramid, 128×128 chunks, already in Web Mercator — and it shows in both halves:\n\n| | Drawing a tile | Measuring an area |\n|---|---|---|\n| This store | 0.22–2.2 s, flat at every zoom | **1.0–1.5 s** |\n| GPCP, no pyramid | 1.2–17.5 s, worse as you zoom out | 6.9–21.1 s |\n\nThe four panels on the right **share a single request**: the table makes it, and the two figures reuse it through the `-- Dashboard --` datasource. One more figure costs zero requests.\n\nThe chain is the same as ever: the map publishes the shape as WKT, a query variable turns it into GeoJSON with DuckDB, and Infinity sends it to `/zarr/statistics` with the same `sel` the layer uses.\n\n**The map's clock is in charge** (`Time range sync: Slider writes variables`): on releasing the bar, the panel writes the window into `mapFrom`/`mapTo`, that recomputes the month, and the three panels refresh. In any other mode the variables are not published and the statistics stay pinned to the end of the dashboard's range.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-2": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "-- Una fila por mes. El store es piramidado (`zarr_levels`), asi que cada zoom\n-- pide su propio nivel; y su eje temporal no son fechas sino enteros 1..12 en\n-- una dimension llamada `month`, de ahi `zarr_time_dim` y `zarr_time_label`.\nSELECT\n  make_timestamp(2020, m, 1, 0, 0, 0)::TIMESTAMPTZ AS time,\n  'https://carbonplan-maps.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/v2/demo/4d/tavg-prec-month' AS zarr_url,\n  'climate'   AS zarr_variable,\n  6           AS zarr_levels,\n  'band=tavg' AS zarr_sel,\n  'month'     AS zarr_time_dim,\n  m::TEXT     AS zarr_time_label\nFROM generate_series(1, 12) t(m)\nORDER BY time"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "id": 2,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Monthly mean temperature · draw an area and drag the time bar",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "ubica-keplergl-panel",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "areaVariable": "area",
                "mapConfig": {
                  "config": {
                    "mapState": {
                      "bearing": 0,
                      "dragRotate": false,
                      "latitude": -8,
                      "longitude": -62,
                      "pitch": 0,
                      "zoom": 3
                    }
                  },
                  "version": "v1"
                },
                "publishWhilePlaying": false,
                "rasterColormap": "magma",
                "rasterServerUrl": "/titiler",
                "showSidePanel": false,
                "timeSync": "variables",
                "timeVariables": {
                  "from": "mapFrom",
                  "to": "mapTo"
                },
                "zarrRescale": "-20,40"
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-3": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "-- Dashboard --"
                      },
                      "group": "datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "panelId": 5
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Reuses the result of the table above: no requests of its own.",
          "id": 3,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Mean temperature in the area",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "stat",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "fixedColor": "green",
                    "mode": "fixed"
                  },
                  "decimals": 1,
                  "unit": "celsius"
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "reduceOptions": {
                  "calcs": [
                    "lastNotNull"
                  ],
                  "fields": "/^media$/",
                  "values": false
                }
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-4": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "-- Dashboard --"
                      },
                      "group": "datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "panelId": 5
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "The warm extreme. Same frame, another field.",
          "id": 4,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Maximum in the area",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "stat",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "fixedColor": "orange",
                    "mode": "fixed"
                  },
                  "decimals": 1,
                  "unit": "celsius"
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "reduceOptions": {
                  "calcs": [
                    "lastNotNull"
                  ],
                  "fields": "/^máx$/",
                  "values": false
                }
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-5": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "infinity"
                      },
                      "group": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "columns": [
                          {
                            "selector": "min",
                            "text": "mín",
                            "type": "number"
                          },
                          {
                            "selector": "max",
                            "text": "máx",
                            "type": "number"
                          },
                          {
                            "selector": "mean",
                            "text": "media",
                            "type": "number"
                          },
                          {
                            "selector": "median",
                            "text": "mediana",
                            "type": "number"
                          },
                          {
                            "selector": "std",
                            "text": "desv",
                            "type": "number"
                          },
                          {
                            "selector": "count",
                            "text": "celdas",
                            "type": "number"
                          }
                        ],
                        "format": "table",
                        "parser": "backend",
                        "root_selector": "properties.statistics.b1",
                        "source": "url",
                        "type": "json",
                        "url": "http://titiler/zarr/statistics?url=${store:percentencode}\u0026variable=climate\u0026group=4\u0026sel=band%3Dtavg\u0026sel=month%3D${mes}",
                        "url_options": {
                          "body_content_type": "application/json",
                          "body_type": "raw",
                          "data": "{\"type\": \"Feature\", \"properties\": {}, \"geometry\": ${zona}}",
                          "method": "POST"
                        }
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": [
                {
                  "group": "organize",
                  "kind": "Transformation",
                  "spec": {
                    "options": {
                      "indexByName": {
                        "celdas": 5,
                        "desv": 4,
                        "media": 2,
                        "mediana": 3,
                        "máx": 1,
                        "mín": 0
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "description": "The dashboard's only POST to /zarr/statistics. The two panels below reuse this result.",
          "id": 5,
          "links": [],
          "title": "The request · every statistic",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "table",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {}
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-6": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "-- Dashboard --"
                      },
                      "group": "datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "panelId": 5
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "The cold extreme, which in a temperature field says as much as the mean: it is where it freezes. Reuses the same frame, without a request of its own.",
          "id": 6,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Minimum in the area",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "stat",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "fixedColor": "blue",
                    "mode": "fixed"
                  },
                  "decimals": 1,
                  "unit": "celsius"
                },
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "reduceOptions": {
                  "calcs": [
                    "lastNotNull"
                  ],
                  "fields": "/^mín$/",
                  "values": false
                }
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "layout": {
      "kind": "GridLayout",
      "spec": {
        "items": [
          {
            "kind": "GridLayoutItem",
            "spec": {
              "element": {
                "kind": "ElementReference",
                "name": "panel-1"
              },
              "height": 11,
              "width": 24,
              "x": 0,
              "y": 0
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "GridLayoutItem",
            "spec": {
              "element": {
                "kind": "ElementReference",
                "name": "panel-2"
              },
              "height": 21,
              "width": 15,
              "x": 0,
              "y": 11
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "GridLayoutItem",
            "spec": {
              "element": {
                "kind": "ElementReference",
                "name": "panel-5"
              },
              "height": 6,
              "width": 9,
              "x": 15,
              "y": 11
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "GridLayoutItem",
            "spec": {
              "element": {
                "kind": "ElementReference",
                "name": "panel-3"
              },
              "height": 5,
              "width": 9,
              "x": 15,
              "y": 17
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "GridLayoutItem",
            "spec": {
              "element": {
                "kind": "ElementReference",
                "name": "panel-6"
              },
              "height": 5,
              "width": 9,
              "x": 15,
              "y": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "GridLayoutItem",
            "spec": {
              "element": {
                "kind": "ElementReference",
                "name": "panel-4"
              },
              "height": 5,
              "width": 9,
              "x": 15,
              "y": 27
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "links": [],
    "liveNow": false,
    "preload": false,
    "tags": [
      "duckdb",
      "infinity",
      "kepler",
      "weather"
    ],
    "timeSettings": {
      "autoRefresh": "",
      "autoRefreshIntervals": [
        "5s",
        "10s",
        "30s",
        "1m",
        "5m",
        "15m",
        "30m",
        "1h",
        "2h",
        "1d"
      ],
      "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
      "from": "2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "hideTimepicker": false,
      "timezone": "utc",
      "to": "2020-07-15T00:00:00.000Z"
    },
    "title": "Monthly mean temperature, measured over an area you draw",
    "variables": [
      {
        "kind": "ConstantVariable",
        "spec": {
          "current": {
            "text": "https://carbonplan-maps.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/v2/demo/4d/tavg-prec-month",
            "value": "https://carbonplan-maps.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/v2/demo/4d/tavg-prec-month"
          },
          "hide": "hideVariable",
          "label": "store",
          "name": "store",
          "query": "https://carbonplan-maps.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/v2/demo/4d/tavg-prec-month",
          "skipUrlSync": false
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "current": {
            "text": "",
            "value": ""
          },
          "hide": "dontHide",
          "label": "Drawn area (WKT)",
          "name": "area",
          "query": "",
          "skipUrlSync": false
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "current": {
            "text": "",
            "value": ""
          },
          "hide": "hideVariable",
          "label": "mapFrom",
          "name": "mapFrom",
          "query": "",
          "skipUrlSync": false
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "TextVariable",
        "spec": {
          "current": {
            "text": "",
            "value": ""
          },
          "hide": "hideVariable",
          "label": "mapTo",
          "name": "mapTo",
          "query": "",
          "skipUrlSync": false
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "QueryVariable",
        "spec": {
          "allowCustomValue": true,
          "current": {
            "text": "",
            "value": ""
          },
          "definition": "-- El mapa publica lo que dibujas como WKT; TiTiler quiere GeoJSON.\n-- OJO: en una consulta de VARIABLE el datasource NO entrecomilla solo (si lo\n-- hace en las de panel), asi que las comillas van a mano. Y el ::VARCHAR no es\n-- cosmetico: sin el, \"unsupported Scan ... map[string]interface{}\".\nLOAD spatial;\nSELECT ST_AsGeoJSON(ST_GeomFromText(\n  coalesce(nullif('${area}', ''), 'POLYGON((-75 -12, -75 2, -50 2, -50 -12, -75 -12))')))::VARCHAR",
          "hide": "hideVariable",
          "includeAll": false,
          "label": "zone",
          "multi": false,
          "name": "zona",
          "options": [],
          "query": {
            "datasource": {
              "name": "duckdb"
            },
            "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
            "kind": "DataQuery",
            "spec": {
              "__legacyStringValue": "-- El mapa publica lo que dibujas como WKT; TiTiler quiere GeoJSON.\n-- OJO: en una consulta de VARIABLE el datasource NO entrecomilla solo (si lo\n-- hace en las de panel), asi que las comillas van a mano. Y el ::VARCHAR no es\n-- cosmetico: sin el, \"unsupported Scan ... map[string]interface{}\".\nLOAD spatial;\nSELECT ST_AsGeoJSON(ST_GeomFromText(\n  coalesce(nullif('${area}', ''), 'POLYGON((-75 -12, -75 2, -50 2, -50 -12, -75 -12))')))::VARCHAR"
            },
            "version": "v0"
          },
          "refresh": "onTimeRangeChanged",
          "regex": "",
          "skipUrlSync": false,
          "sort": "disabled"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "QueryVariable",
        "spec": {
          "allowCustomValue": true,
          "current": {
            "text": "",
            "value": ""
          },
          "definition": "-- El mes que el mapa esta pintando. `mapTo` lo publica el propio panel al\n-- mover la barra de tiempo, y el store responde a un entero, no a una fecha.\nSELECT extract(month FROM coalesce(try_cast(nullif('${mapTo}', '') AS TIMESTAMPTZ),\n                                   $__timeTo()::TIMESTAMPTZ) AT TIME ZONE 'UTC')::INTEGER::VARCHAR",
          "hide": "dontHide",
          "includeAll": false,
          "label": "Month measured",
          "multi": false,
          "name": "mes",
          "options": [],
          "query": {
            "datasource": {
              "name": "duckdb"
            },
            "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
            "kind": "DataQuery",
            "spec": {
              "__legacyStringValue": "-- El mes que el mapa esta pintando. `mapTo` lo publica el propio panel al\n-- mover la barra de tiempo, y el store responde a un entero, no a una fecha.\nSELECT extract(month FROM coalesce(try_cast(nullif('${mapTo}', '') AS TIMESTAMPTZ),\n                                   $__timeTo()::TIMESTAMPTZ) AT TIME ZONE 'UTC')::INTEGER::VARCHAR"
            },
            "version": "v0"
          },
          "refresh": "onTimeRangeChanged",
          "regex": "",
          "skipUrlSync": false,
          "sort": "disabled"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}